  'cata-codeta-agree-calm-mediation-begins-2026-11-02',
  'Rival taxi bodies CATA and CODETA agree to calm as mediation starts',
  'Traffic', '2026-11-02', 'Cape Town Etc', 'https://www.capetownetc.com/news/cata-and-codeta-agree-to-a-week-of-calm-amid-taxi-violence/',
  'After a meeting on 2 November, the two Cape taxi associations agreed to stop the violence and enter facilitated mediation with the provincial government and the City.',
  'Two rival minibus-taxi groups, CATA and CODETA, have promised a spell of calm while mediation begins, after weeks of violent clashes over routes in parts of the Western Cape.

The agreement came out of a meeting on 2 November that brought both associations together with provincial officials, City officials and the regional taxi council, SANTACO. Reports say the dispute centred on routes in Delft, Langa and Epping, and that the unrest claimed 12 lives and disrupted Cape Town International Airport on the previous Friday.

Both associations committed to ending the violence and to working with independent facilitators to deal with the underlying causes. According to Cape Town Etc, the first stage involves separate sessions between each association and City and provincial officials, with SANTACO observing, so that each side can raise its concerns and name its priority issues. Once those sessions are done, all parties are to meet again to look for solutions that both associations can accept. A follow-up meeting with government is planned for the following week.

The provincial authorities had earlier obtained an interim court order against both associations. Police and law enforcement are monitoring ranks and routes, and taxi services have resumed.

Commuters are advised to rely on verified information from official channels for updates on affected routes, as SANTACO has urged.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
